        return a + b + c;
    }

    public static int sum(int... numbers) {
        int total = 0;
        if (numbers != null) {
            for (int n : numbers) {
                total += n;
            }
        }
        return total;
    }
}
```
*Note: Providing the 2-argument and 3-argument overloads prevents the JVM from allocating a heap array when callers only pass 2 or 3 numbers!*
</details>

